# Escape exiles three *other* cards from the graveyard (CR 702.138a). Faithless Looting, paid with Mox Ruby, discards the
# Challenger and an Island, so on turn 3 the graveyard holds the Challenger plus only two others (Looting and the Island).
# Gold Pan makes an untapped Treasure. Three Moxen and Sol Ring then float {R}{G}{W}{C}{C}, enough for {3}{R}{G}, while the
# Treasure stays untapped: its mana ability must not be read as a way to feed the escape's exile cost, so the cast is
# refused. The positive control, with three others, is bloodbraid-challenger-escapes-exiling-three-other-cards-then-cascades-and-attacks.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Faithless Looting
Bloodbraid Challenger
Sol Ring
Island
Gold Pan
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Faithless Looting.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Bloodbraid Challenger; Island)
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 3
Bot1.Hand.Gold Pan.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
? Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token.Tapped = false
! Bot1.Graveyard.Bloodbraid Challenger.Cast(Ability: Escape)

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 3
Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token.Tapped = false
